    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "315 Montgomery Street\nSan Francisco\nSeptember 21, 1929\nLt. Col. Gerald C. Brandt\nCrissy Field\nSan Francisco, California.\nMy dear Colonel Brandt:\nAs a result of the conference of our Committee a\nfew days ago,\nI en sending three copies of the joint\nreport of our Committee to you.\nI will ask that you and\nMr. Mouton sign each of these three copies and that you\nme11 the original to Milo H, Kent, Chairman of the Airport\nComnittee of the Board of Supervisors, irmediately.\nhave already signed the three copies which I enclose to\nyou•\nThe other two copies are for you and it. Mouton.\nAs I will not be back from Europe until about\nDecember 10th,\nI am very anzious that the dirport Committee\nof the Board of Supervisors have our full report in their\nhands, because it explains in detail,\nthe position consist-\nently\ntaken by our Advisory Comnittee.\nWith best regards and good wishes, I am\nSincerely,\n(Signed) BILI"
    ],
